<div class="dsl-wrap">

  <div class="dsl-intro">
    <p>This diagram maps BSTA courses (and a few related non-BSTA courses) onto a standard data science lifecycle, based on a working draft curriculum-mapping exercise. Each course may not cover every stage &mdash; as students move from foundational to advanced courses, coverage of the lifecycle expands. The outer ring names cross-cutting practice dimensions (fairness, transparency, generalizability, sustainability, accountability) that apply across every stage.</p>
    <p class="dsl-note">Hover or tap a lifecycle stage (or its course badge) to see which courses cover it, plus any curriculum gap or idea flagged for that stage. Hover the outer ring labels for related notes. This is a working draft, not an official curriculum document.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="dsl-legend">
    <span class="dsl-legend-item"><span class="dsl-swatch primary"></span> Primary coverage</span>
    <span class="dsl-legend-item"><span class="dsl-swatch related"></span> Related / partial coverage</span>
    <span class="dsl-legend-item"><span class="dsl-swatch gap"></span> Possible gap</span>
    <span class="dsl-legend-item"><span class="dsl-swatch ethics"></span> Cross-cutting dimension</span>
  </div>

  <div class="dsl-stage-wrap">
    <div class="dsl-diagram-holder">
      <svg id="dsl-svg" viewBox="0 0 900 900" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="Data science lifecycle diagram"></svg>
    </div>
    <div class="dsl-panel" id="dsl-panel">
      <h3 id="dsl-panel-title">Explore the lifecycle</h3>
      <p class="dsl-panel-hint" id="dsl-panel-hint">Hover or tap any stage on the wheel, a course badge, or an outer-ring label to see details here.</p>
      <div id="dsl-panel-body"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="dsl-note" style="margin-top:1rem;">
    <strong>Course key:</strong> BSTA 511, 512, and 513 are the required applied sequence (Estimation &amp; Hypothesis Testing, Linear Models, Categorical Data Analysis). "PUBH 523" is Introduction to R, the cross-program course this curriculum-mapping project was developed for. "BMI 525" is a Biomedical Informatics course outside the BSTA prefix. Full BSTA course descriptions are on the <a href="compentencies.qmd">Competencies</a> page.
  </div>

